<title>USA: Amscan Holdings chairman dies.</title>
<headline>Amscan Holdings chairman dies.</headline>
<dateline>ELMSFORD, N.Y. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amscan Holdings Inc on Wednesday said its founder and chairman, John Svenningsen, died Tuesday night after a long illness.</p>
<p>A company spokeswoman said Svenningsen was 66. No replacement has been named, she added.</p>
<p>Amscan is a leading supplier of party goods, such as paper plates, cups, napkins and tablecovers, which are sold through more than 20,000 retail outlets in the United States.</p>
